[sub_resource type="RectangleShape2D" id="RectangleShape2D_kill"]
size = Vector2(8000, 40)

; Two chimneys of rising air (issue #143: #52's WindZone pointed up, plus
; #18's CrumblingLedge). Gale's wind blows across; here it blows up.
;
; **Ground.** A low core in the middle (x=-160..160, top y=320) and two
; higher banks (x=+-420..+-740, top y=280). Between them are two 260 px
; shafts, too wide to walk and open to the kill zone.
;
; **Updrafts.** Each shaft has an upward gust (x=+-160..+-420, y=-170..470).
; They use the part's default cycle: 2.5 s calm, 1 s tell, 1.5 s gust. The
; two shafts are half a cycle apart, so one is always about to blow.
; strength 1900 is a little over the player's gravity (1470): a gust stops a
; fall and lifts slowly, up to around y=-190, well inside the -450 top edge.
; Falling into a shaft during a gust is a second chance; falling into it
; while it is calm is a ring-out.
;
; **Perches.** A crumbling ledge sits high over each shaft (x=+-210..+-370,
; top y=-72) with a pickup on it. An updraft is the easy way up, and the
; ledge drops you back into the shaft soon after.
;
; Spawns: four on the core, two on each bank, all clear of the shafts. The
; outer ends of the banks are open sky and ring out.

; Backdrop (issue #117): cold, high air over a range.
